WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.260
I sort of went back and forth about whether
to even do this story because there is so

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.600
much resistance

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.940
since now to any Russia related news.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.269
Either you already understand what happened
or you've totally bought into the witch hunt

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:14.690
conspiracy theory type stuff.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.929
So I really was unsure about whether to even
talk about this.

00:00:16.929 --> 00:00:20.760
But in the end, this is actually really big
news and I decided it was an important story

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.760
to do.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.169
The Senate intelligence committee, which is
controlled by Republicans in a new report

00:00:27.169 --> 00:00:34.020
has found that the Kremlin directed Russia's
social media meddling in the 2016 election

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.690
period and this is, it's becoming, or it should
be a post partisan issue.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:46.030
The Republican led Senate intelligence committee
has a long list of recommendations for Congress

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:51.730
and for Donald Trump and for social media
companies to prevent the same thing from happening

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:58.750
in 2020 but we've already seen Senate majority
leader Moscow, Mitch McConnell block every

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.829
single effort to prevent 2020 meddling.

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:03.239
So it's going to be an uphill battle.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:10.010
The report suggests that social media companies
add transparency to the sources of political

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:18.640
advertisements on their platforms, that they
notify users about exposure to misinformation

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.060
and hilariously, hilariously, in a depressing
sense, the panel report recommends that the

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:31.221
Trump administration remind voters about the
dangers of foreign interference in 2020 I

00:01:31.221 --> 00:01:33.120
laughed out loud when I read that.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.120
How quaint, right?

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:40.190
The Trump administration should really warn
people that warn people that they benefit

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.190
from it.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.710
They have no interest in stopping it.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:44.570
Why on earth would they warn people?

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:49.259
This is the whole problem that we're dealing
with in many of the techniques and the players

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:52.380
that are mentioned in the report were already
known to us.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.030
They talk about the IRA, the internet research
agency.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.770
They were a big player.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:00.560
They talk about one strategy that we knew
about which was to target black Americans,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.420
particularly in parts of the country like
Baltimore and Ferguson, Missouri, which were

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:09.940
experiencing racial unrest and priests specifically
target those areas, black voters in those

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.220
areas to foment more racial unrest.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.860
The real news here is not any of that.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.610
We knew all of that stuff.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.480
The news is that we've learned that the Kremlin
itself was directing it and that conclusion

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.450
was reached not by, you know, whoever Trump
claims it was reached by.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:32.630
It was reached by a bipartisan panel that
is led and controlled by Republicans, not

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:36.360
a partisan democratic hack job or whatever.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.670
Trump will obviously claim.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:43.940
Now let's do the normal disclaimers here because
I think that this is where maybe some on the

